  "intent": {
    "task": "For every supplied recurrence, give both early terms and a general formula, distinguishing additive from multiplicative growth and respecting index 1.",
    "source_solution": "a) Starting at 10, n-1 increments of 10 give 10+10(n-1)=10n. At n=1 this is 10; replacing n with n+1 increases it by 10.\nb) There are n-1 multiplications after the initial factor 10: 10*10^(n-1)=10^n. At n=1 the formula gives 10, and successive terms have ratio 10.\nc) 2+2(n-1)=2n; the first five terms are 2,4,6,8,10. The formula has initial value 2 and constant successive difference 2.\nd) 2*2^(n-1)=2^n; the first five terms are 2,4,8,16,32. The initial value is 2 and each successive ratio is 2.",
    "unit_reason": "Each response is a complete prefix-plus-formula pair. Multiple selection compares all four initial-value rules in one coherent task; matching only an early coincidence, particularly 2,4, does not settle a formula.",
    "concept_blocks": [
      7,
      8,
      9,
      10
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Selecting a complete prefix does not demonstrate independently writing the sequence.",
      "Selecting a prefix and formula does not demonstrate independently constructing a general term.",
      "The source asks for the first few terms without fixing their number; five is an explicit condition of this authored question only."
    ],
    "figure_observations": []
